#. ja: ミニオン「ゴールドラッシュ」を呼び出す。<br>小さなトロッコ玩具。夢は一攫千金
#. de: Du rufst deine Goldrausch-Karre als Begleiter herbei. Das Gold musst du aber selber hineinschaufeln.
#. fr: Vous appelez votre mascotte chariot de mine mécanique.<br>* La pépite d'or qu'il transporte n'a aucune valeur dans le monde réel.
#. column 1: Unbeknownst to their clients, retainers across Eorzea have been secretly using these automated minecarts to help haul about all the materials adventurers have them venture forth to collect. As of yet, however, no adventurer has reported receiving a “rush of gold.”
#. column 2: But I don't want to<br>work in the silver mines!<br>   - Gold Saucer Patron
#. column 3: 24 Karat
#. column 4: Instantly restores damaged ally Shield.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:154:0:0"
msgid "Summon your gold rush minecart minion. It is, unsurprisingly, void of gold."
msgstr "Призывает миньона «Золотая лихорадка». Как ни странно, золота в вагонетке нет."

#. ja: からくり仕掛けの小さなトロッコ。リテイナーが仕事中に得た品を運ぶために、連れ歩いていたものらしい。しかし、ある時、巨大な金鉱石を発見し乗せてみたところ、頑なに手放そうとしなくなったという。結構、がめつい
#. de: Was kein Abenteurer ahnt, ist, dass Gehilfen seit langem automatisierte Karren benutzen, um die Früchte ihrer Streifzüge abzutransportieren.
#. fr: Ce petit chariot était utilisé par un servant pour transporter des objets au cours de son travail. Mais lorsqu'il trouva une pépite d'or géante, le chariot refusa de la lâcher.
#. column 0: Summon your gold rush minecart minion. It is, unsurprisingly, void of gold.
#. column 2: But I don't want to<br>work in the silver mines!<br>   - Gold Saucer Patron
#. column 3: 24 Karat
#. column 4: Instantly restores damaged ally Shield.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:154:0:1"
msgid "Unbeknownst to their clients, retainers across Eorzea have been secretly using these automated minecarts to help haul about all the materials adventurers have them venture forth to collect. As of yet, however, no adventurer has reported receiving a “rush of gold.”"
msgstr "Слуги по всему Эорзеи, сами того не говоря хозяевам, тайком используют такие вагонетки, чтобы перевозить добытые по поручению искателей приключений материалы. Но пока ни один искатель не сообщал, что получил «золотую лихорадку»."

#. ja: キラキラ☆
#. de: Ah, ein neuer Kandidat für<br>die Arbeiten im Bergwerk?<br><i>Beringaer</i>
#. fr: Cling<nbsp>! Cling<nbsp>! Cling<nbsp>!
#. column 0: Summon your gold rush minecart minion. It is, unsurprisingly, void of gold.
#. column 1: Unbeknownst to their clients, retainers across Eorzea have been secretly using these automated minecarts to help haul about all the materials adventurers have them venture forth to collect. As of yet, however, no adventurer has reported receiving a “rush of gold.”
#. column 3: 24 Karat
#. column 4: Instantly restores damaged ally Shield.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:154:0:2"
msgid "But I don't want to<br>work in the silver mines!<br>   - Gold Saucer Patron"
msgstr "Но я не хочу<br>работать в серебряных шахтах!<br>   — Посетитель Золотого блекджеку"

#. ja: 金メッキ
#. de: Neuvergoldung
#. fr: Redorer son blason
#. column 0: Summon your gold rush minecart minion. It is, unsurprisingly, void of gold.
#. column 1: Unbeknownst to their clients, retainers across Eorzea have been secretly using these automated minecarts to help haul about all the materials adventurers have them venture forth to collect. As of yet, however, no adventurer has reported receiving a “rush of gold.”
#. column 2: But I don't want to<br>work in the silver mines!<br>   - Gold Saucer Patron
#. column 4: Instantly restores damaged ally Shield.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:154:0:3"
msgid "24 Karat"
msgstr "Двадцатичетырёхкаратная"

#. ja: シールドが破壊されていた場合、復活させる。
#. de: Stellt einen zerstörten Schild wieder her.
#. fr: Rétablit votre bouclier s'il a été détruit.
#. column 0: Summon your gold rush minecart minion. It is, unsurprisingly, void of gold.
#. column 1: Unbeknownst to their clients, retainers across Eorzea have been secretly using these automated minecarts to help haul about all the materials adventurers have them venture forth to collect. As of yet, however, no adventurer has reported receiving a “rush of gold.”
#. column 2: But I don't want to<br>work in the silver mines!<br>   - Gold Saucer Patron
#. column 3: 24 Karat
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:154:0:4"
msgid "Instantly restores damaged ally Shield. "
msgstr "Мгновенно восстанавливает разрушенный союзный щит."

#. ja: ミニオン「ザ・プライモグズ」を呼び出す。<br>モーグリ魔法人形によるバックバンド。演奏はニガテ
#. de: Du rufst deine Primog-Kapelle als Begleiter herbei. Die <i>einzige</i> mechanische Kapelle diesseits des Schwarztee-Bachs ... Und somit die <i>beste</i> mechanische Kapelle diesseits des Schwarztee-Bachs.
#. fr: Vous appelez votre mascotte fanfares des Primogs. Les <i>seuls</i> automates musiciens de ce côté du ruisseau du Thé noir. Ce qui fait d'eux les <i>meilleurs</i> automates musiciens de ce côté du ruisseau du Thé noir.
#. column 1: One night, an aspiring moogle bard had a dream─a dream to become the greatest musician in all the realm. But to do it he would need a band of merry moogles to accompany him. The bard had no friends, so instead he decided to create his own band from stolen mammet parts.
#. column 2: Off with their heads!<br>   - Good King Moggle Mog XII
#. column 3: Moogle Madhouse
#. column 4: Increases ATK of all allies within range by 20 (40 if the ally is a <ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>poppet</ui-edge-color></ui-color>).<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Duration:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 6s
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:155:0:0"
msgid "Summon your set of Primogs minion, the <i>only</i> mechanical musicians this side of Black Tea Brook...making them the <i>greatest</i> mechanical musicians this side of Black Tea Brook."
msgstr "Призывает миньонов Примогов — <i>единственных</i> механических музыкантов по эту сторону Чёрного Чайного ручья... а значит, <i>величайших</i> механических музыкантов по эту сторону Чёрного Чайного ручья."

#. ja: 吟遊詩人バンドの結成を夢見たモーグリが、バックバンド代わりに作った魔法人形。小さな楽器を作ったところまでは良かったが、演奏させることは意外と難しかった。なお、バンドは音楽性の違いにより、デビュー前に解散した
#. de: Ein nach Erfolg trachtender Mogry-Barde erkannte, dass Zuhörer seine Stimme eher zu schätzen geneigt sind, wenn er von einer lautstarken Kapelle begleitet wird. Also baute er sich eine aus alten Marionettenteilen.
#. fr: Ce groupe d'automates d'accompagnement fut créé par des Mogs qui rêvaient de former un groupe de bardes. À présent, il faut faire en sorte qu'ils jouent juste... En raison de “différences artistiques”, le groupe n'a jamais fait ses débuts.
#. column 0: Summon your set of Primogs minion, the <i>only</i> mechanical musicians this side of Black Tea Brook...making them the <i>greatest</i> mechanical musicians this side of Black Tea Brook.
#. column 2: Off with their heads!<br>   - Good King Moggle Mog XII
#. column 3: Moogle Madhouse
#. column 4: Increases ATK of all allies within range by 20 (40 if the ally is a <ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>poppet</ui-edge-color></ui-color>).<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Duration:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 6s
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:155:0:1"
msgid "One night, an aspiring moogle bard had a dream─a dream to become the greatest musician in all the realm. But to do it he would need a band of merry moogles to accompany him. The bard had no friends, so instead he decided to create his own band from stolen mammet parts."
msgstr "Однажды ночью начинающий моогл-барда осенила мечта — стать величайшим музыкантом во всём мире. Для этого ему нужна была весёлая группа мооглов, которая ему подыграет. Друзей у барда не было, и он решил собрать группу из украденных деталей мамметов."

#. ja: ♪♪♪
#. de: Schlagt ihnen die Köpfe ab! Allen!<br><i>König Mogul Mog XII.</i>
#. fr: ♪♪♪
