#. ja: ミニオン「ミニギガテンダー」を呼び出す。<br>ギガテンダーの若木。大きいのか小さいのかハッキリしない
#. de: Du rufst deinen Mini-Riesenkaktor als Begleiter herbei.<br>Er hat die richtige Größe, um ihn als Hocker zu verwenden, aber das wäre wohl eine sehr schlechte Idee.
#. fr: Vous appelez votre mascotte mini-gigapampa, qui semble lui-même confus par sa propre taille... Est-il mini ou giga<nbsp>?
#. column 1: Though known for their prodigious size, gigantenders come into the world small and grow ever so slowly. This creature is estimated to be between twenty and thirty years of age, which by gigantender standards is still considered young. The oldest known creatures are said to live beyond two centuries.
#. column 2: In another three hundred years,<br>I'll be bigger and stronger<br>than you will ever be!<br>   - Ohl Deeh
#. column 3: 1000 Flowers
#. column 4: Delivers 8% damage to the nearest enemy Arcana Stone.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:338:0:0"
msgid "Summon your micro gigantender minion. Is it small or is it big? You be the judge."
msgstr "Призвать миньона — микро-гигантендера. Он маленький или большой? Решай сам."

#. ja: ギガテンダーの若木。巨大なことで知られる種だが、当然ながら発芽直後は小さく、少しずつ成長する。この個体は、樹齢20～30年程と推定されるが、それでも若木の部類。一説では200年以上、生きる個体もいるのだとか
#. de: Riesenkaktoren sind natürlich für ihre riesige Größe bekannt, doch alles, was groß wird, muss mal klein anfangen. Dieses Exemplar ist grob geschätzt erst 20 bis 30 Jahre alt und hat noch über 150 Jahre Wachstum vor sich.
#. fr: Jeune gigapampa, animal célèbre pour sa taille adulte immense. Celui-ci n'a que trente ans, et est donc encore adolescent, car certains d'entre eux pourraient atteindre l'âge vénérable de deux cents ans.
#. column 0: Summon your micro gigantender minion. Is it small or is it big? You be the judge.
#. column 2: In another three hundred years,<br>I'll be bigger and stronger<br>than you will ever be!<br>   - Ohl Deeh
#. column 3: 1000 Flowers
#. column 4: Delivers 8% damage to the nearest enemy Arcana Stone.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:338:0:1"
msgid "Though known for their prodigious size, gigantenders come into the world small and grow ever so slowly. This creature is estimated to be between twenty and thirty years of age, which by gigantender standards is still considered young. The oldest known creatures are said to live beyond two centuries."
msgstr "Гигантендеры славятся огромным размером, но рождаются крошечными и растут очень медленно. Этому, по оценкам, от двадцати до тридцати лет, а по меркам гигантендеров он всё ещё молод. Говорят, самые старые живут больше двух столетий."

#. ja: 針百万本！
#. de: 100.000 Nadeln!
#. fr: Un million d'épines<nbsp>!
#. column 0: Summon your micro gigantender minion. Is it small or is it big? You be the judge.
#. column 1: Though known for their prodigious size, gigantenders come into the world small and grow ever so slowly. This creature is estimated to be between twenty and thirty years of age, which by gigantender standards is still considered young. The oldest known creatures are said to live beyond two centuries.
#. column 3: 1000 Flowers
#. column 4: Delivers 8% damage to the nearest enemy Arcana Stone.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:338:0:2"
msgid "In another three hundred years,<br>I'll be bigger and stronger<br>than you will ever be!<br>   - Ohl Deeh"
msgstr "Через триста лет<br>я стану больше и сильнее,<br>чем ты когда-либо будешь!<br>   — Ол Дих"

#. ja: 花千本！
#. de: 1000 Blumen!
#. fr: Millefleur
#. column 0: Summon your micro gigantender minion. Is it small or is it big? You be the judge.
#. column 1: Though known for their prodigious size, gigantenders come into the world small and grow ever so slowly. This creature is estimated to be between twenty and thirty years of age, which by gigantender standards is still considered young. The oldest known creatures are said to live beyond two centuries.
#. column 2: In another three hundred years,<br>I'll be bigger and stronger<br>than you will ever be!<br>   - Ohl Deeh
#. column 4: Delivers 8% damage to the nearest enemy Arcana Stone.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:338:0:3"
msgid "1000 Flowers"
msgstr "Тысяча игл"

#. ja: 最も近い敵軍のアルカナストーンに、8%のダメージを与える。
#. de: Fügt dem nächstgelegenen gegnerischen Arkana-Stein 8 % Schaden zu.
#. fr: Inflige des dégâts équivalents à 8% de sa solidité à la pierre arcanique ennemie la plus proche.
#. column 0: Summon your micro gigantender minion. Is it small or is it big? You be the judge.
#. column 1: Though known for their prodigious size, gigantenders come into the world small and grow ever so slowly. This creature is estimated to be between twenty and thirty years of age, which by gigantender standards is still considered young. The oldest known creatures are said to live beyond two centuries.
#. column 2: In another three hundred years,<br>I'll be bigger and stronger<br>than you will ever be!<br>   - Ohl Deeh
#. column 3: 1000 Flowers
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:338:0:4"
msgid "Delivers 8% damage to the nearest enemy Arcana Stone."
msgstr "Наносит ближайшему вражескому арканному камню урон в размере 8% его прочности."

#. ja: ミニオン「クリオニッド・ラーヴァ」を呼び出す。<br>クリオニッドの幼生。食欲旺盛なお年頃
#. de: Du rufst deine Clionidenlarve als Begleiter herbei.<br>Clioniden können bereits im Larvenstadium fliegen und haben einen sehr gesunden Appetit.
#. fr: Vous appelez votre mascotte jeune clionide, qui est pile dans la tranche d'âge où son appétit est insatiable.
#. column 1: A relative of the sea slug, the clionid feeds on plankton early in life. As it matures, however, it begins consuming flesh in order to satisfy its voracious appetite, and uses the tentacles extending from its head to latch onto prey. For now it follows you obediently. For now...
#. column 2: What a delicious morsel!<br>I wanna get my tentacles<br>around her...<br>   - Ultros
#. column 3: Buccal Cones
#. column 4: Reduces HP of enemy Search Eye by 90%. No effect if Search Eye is already inoperable.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:339:0:0"
msgid "Summon your clionid larva minion, small on size but massive on appetite."
msgstr "Призвать миньона — личинку клиониды. Маленькая, зато аппетит огромный."

#. ja: クリオニッドの幼生。実は巻貝の仲間で、生まれてしばらくは植物プランクトンをこし取って食べるが、やがて肉食に変じて、頭頂部の触手で獲物を捕獲するようになるという。だが、今は従順に後ろをついてくる。今はまだ……
#. de: Wer hätte gedacht, dass Clioniden zur Gattung der Kreiselschnecken gehören? Nach dem Schlüpfen ernähren sie sich zuerst von Plankton, bis die Tentakel auf ihrem Kopf stark genug sind, größere Beute zu fangen.
#. fr: À ce stade de sa croissance, cette clionide se nourrit uniquement de plancton. Elle deviendra carnivore en grandissant, et se servira du tentacule qu'elle a sur la tête pour attraper ses proies. Lorsque ce moment arrivera, elle risque de ne plus vous être aussi obéissante...
#. column 0: Summon your clionid larva minion, small on size but massive on appetite.
#. column 2: What a delicious morsel!<br>I wanna get my tentacles<br>around her...<br>   - Ultros
#. column 3: Buccal Cones
#. column 4: Reduces HP of enemy Search Eye by 90%. No effect if Search Eye is already inoperable.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:339:0:1"
msgid "A relative of the sea slug, the clionid feeds on plankton early in life. As it matures, however, it begins consuming flesh in order to satisfy its voracious appetite, and uses the tentacles extending from its head to latch onto prey. For now it follows you obediently. For now..."
msgstr "Клионида — родственница морского слизня. В начале жизни она питается планктоном, но взрослея, переходит на мясо, чтобы утолить прожорливый аппетит. Добычу она хватает щупальцами, растущими у неё на голове. Пока что она послушно следует за тобой. Пока что..."

#. ja: パカッ！
#. de: \<schmoll>
#. fr: Paka<nbsp>!
#. column 0: Summon your clionid larva minion, small on size but massive on appetite.
#. column 1: A relative of the sea slug, the clionid feeds on plankton early in life. As it matures, however, it begins consuming flesh in order to satisfy its voracious appetite, and uses the tentacles extending from its head to latch onto prey. For now it follows you obediently. For now...
#. column 3: Buccal Cones
#. column 4: Reduces HP of enemy Search Eye by 90%. No effect if Search Eye is already inoperable.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:339:0:2"
msgid "What a delicious morsel!<br>I wanna get my tentacles<br>around her...<br>   - Ultros"
msgstr "Какой аппетитный кусочек!<br>Так бы и обвил её<br>своими щупальцами...<br>   — Ультрос"

#. ja: バッカルコーン
#. de: Bukkale Kegel
#. fr: Cônes buccaux
#. column 0: Summon your clionid larva minion, small on size but massive on appetite.
#. column 1: A relative of the sea slug, the clionid feeds on plankton early in life. As it matures, however, it begins consuming flesh in order to satisfy its voracious appetite, and uses the tentacles extending from its head to latch onto prey. For now it follows you obediently. For now...
#. column 2: What a delicious morsel!<br>I wanna get my tentacles<br>around her...<br>   - Ultros
#. column 4: Reduces HP of enemy Search Eye by 90%. No effect if Search Eye is already inoperable.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:339:0:3"
msgid "Buccal Cones"
msgstr "Ротовые конусы"

#. ja: 敵軍のサーチ・アイへ90%のダメージを与える。すでに破壊されている場合は効果はない。
#. de: Fügt einem gegnerischen Suchenden Auge 90 % Schaden zu. Kein Effekt, falls es schon zerstört ist.
#. fr: Inflige des dégâts équivalents à 90% de sa solidité à l'œil scrutateur ennemi. N'a aucun effet si ce dernier est déjà détruit.
#. column 0: Summon your clionid larva minion, small on size but massive on appetite.
#. column 1: A relative of the sea slug, the clionid feeds on plankton early in life. As it matures, however, it begins consuming flesh in order to satisfy its voracious appetite, and uses the tentacles extending from its head to latch onto prey. For now it follows you obediently. For now...
#. column 2: What a delicious morsel!<br>I wanna get my tentacles<br>around her...<br>   - Ultros
#. column 3: Buccal Cones
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:339:0:4"
msgid "Reduces HP of enemy Search Eye by 90%. No effect if Search Eye is already inoperable."
msgstr "Снижает HP вражеского Ока наблюдателя на 90%. Не действует, если Око уже уничтожено."

#. ja: ミニオン「タイニーダックビル」を呼び出す。<br>カモノハシの幼獣。足装備ではない
#. de: Du rufst dein Baby-Schnabeltier als Begleiter herbei.<br>Es hat zwar fast dieselbe Größe, sollte aber keinesfalls mit einem Schnabelschuh verwechselt werden!
#. fr: Vous appelez votre mascotte ornithorynque nain, à ne pas confondre avec une vieille chaussure.
#. column 1: Named for its duck-like bill, this creature hunts not by sight or smell, but rather by sensing the aetheric discharge from prey. It can also deliver a potent venom from the spurs on its hindfeet, causing great pain if not death─a sobering contrast to its adorable appearance.
#. column 2: Aren't you just the most<br>adorable little thing!?<br>    - Jessie
#. column 3: Venomous Spurs
#. column 4: Delivers 20 points of damage every second to all enemies within range.<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Duration:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 15s
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:340:0:0"
msgid "Summon your bitty duckbill minion. Do not attempt to put on your feet."
msgstr "Призвать миньона — крошечного утконоса. На ноги не надевать."

#. ja: カモノハシの幼獣。名の由来でもあるカモに似たくちばしは、獲物の生体電流を感知する感覚器のようなもので、視覚に頼らず狩りを行うことができる。また、後ろ脚に毒を分泌する蹴爪を持つなど、意外と凶悪な性質を備える
#. de: Dieses possierliche Tierchen hat einen Schnabel, der an den einer Ente erinnert. Mit diesem unge-<br>wöhnlichen Sinnesorgan kann es Beutetiere aufspüren, selbst wenn es diese nicht sehen kann. Vorsicht: Es besitzt einen giftigen Stachel am Hinterbein.
#. fr: Le bec de cet animal lui permet de ressentir le moindre courant électrique émis par ses proies, ce qui l'aide à chasser même quand il ne voit rien. De plus, ses griffes arrières sécrètent un poison violent, ce qui en fait un animal plutôt agressif malgré son air un peu ballot.
#. column 0: Summon your bitty duckbill minion. Do not attempt to put on your feet.
#. column 2: Aren't you just the most<br>adorable little thing!?<br>    - Jessie
#. column 3: Venomous Spurs
#. column 4: Delivers 20 points of damage every second to all enemies within range.<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Duration:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 15s
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:340:0:1"
msgid "Named for its duck-like bill, this creature hunts not by sight or smell, but rather by sensing the aetheric discharge from prey. It can also deliver a potent venom from the spurs on its hindfeet, causing great pain if not death─a sobering contrast to its adorable appearance."
msgstr "Утконос получил своё имя за похожий на утиный клюв. Он охотится не зрением и не обонянием, а улавливая эфирные разряды добычи. А ещё ядовитые шпоры на задних лапах могут причинить жуткую боль, а то и убить. Вот тебе и милый зверёк."

#. ja: クルル、グルルル…
#. de: \<guruuu>
#. fr: Grr grrrrrr<nbsp>!
#. column 0: Summon your bitty duckbill minion. Do not attempt to put on your feet.
#. column 1: Named for its duck-like bill, this creature hunts not by sight or smell, but rather by sensing the aetheric discharge from prey. It can also deliver a potent venom from the spurs on its hindfeet, causing great pain if not death─a sobering contrast to its adorable appearance.
#. column 3: Venomous Spurs
#. column 4: Delivers 20 points of damage every second to all enemies within range.<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Duration:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 15s
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:340:0:2"
msgid "Aren't you just the most<br>adorable little thing!?<br>    - Jessie"
msgstr "Ну разве ты не самое<br>милое создание на свете!?<br>   — Джесси"

#. ja: 毒の蹴爪
#. de: Giftstachel
#. fr: Griffes empoisonnées
#. column 0: Summon your bitty duckbill minion. Do not attempt to put on your feet.
#. column 1: Named for its duck-like bill, this creature hunts not by sight or smell, but rather by sensing the aetheric discharge from prey. It can also deliver a potent venom from the spurs on its hindfeet, causing great pain if not death─a sobering contrast to its adorable appearance.
