#. ja: ミニオン「ダイヴァディーパ」を呼び出す。<br>ムリガ神群の一柱、ダイヴァディーパを模した魔法神像
#. de: Du rufst deine Daivadipa-Puppe als Begleiter herbei. Knie dich nieder, sieh ihr in die Augen und erfahre, auf welcher Seite du stehst.
#. fr: Vous appelez votre mascotte Daïvadipa miniature, une poupée magique à l'effigie d'une divinité mrga.
#. column 1: A mechanical image of Daivadipa, one of the Mrga traditionally worshipped in Thavnair. In the old tongue of the Arkasodara, his name means “heavenly light” or simply “eye”─a reference to his ability to discern good and evil.
#. column 2: Naught will escape my<br>all-seeing eyes, no, no.<br>   - Gyoka
#. column 3: Divine Eye
#. column 4: Increases ATK of all allies within range by 10.<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Duration:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 10s
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:442:0:0"
msgid "Summon your wind-up Daivadipa minion. Can discern good and evil─so long as they are at knee height."
msgstr "Призовите заводного ДайвадИпу. Он отличает добро от зла — если они не выше колена."

#. ja: サベネア島で古来より信仰されてきたムリガ神群の一柱、ダイヴァディーパを模した魔法神像。その名は、アルカソーダラ族の古語で「天の灯火」、あるいは「眼」という意味があり、この神が善悪の真理を見通すことを示している
#. de: Eine Puppe in der Gestalt von einer der Mrga-Gottheiten. In der Sprache der alten Arkasodara bedeutet der Name „himmlisches Licht“ sowie „Auge“, was eine Referenz zu ihrer Fähigkeit darstellt, Gutes von Bösem zu unterscheiden.
#. fr: Daïvadipa est une divinité mrga vénérée par les Thavnairois depuis de nombreuses générations. En langue arkasodara ancienne, son nom signifie à la fois “lumière divine” et “œil”, en référence à sa capacité à distinguer le bien du mal.
#. column 0: Summon your wind-up Daivadipa minion. Can discern good and evil─so long as they are at knee height.
#. column 2: Naught will escape my<br>all-seeing eyes, no, no.<br>   - Gyoka
#. column 3: Divine Eye
#. column 4: Increases ATK of all allies within range by 10.<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Duration:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 10s
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:442:0:1"
msgid "A mechanical image of Daivadipa, one of the Mrga traditionally worshipped in Thavnair. In the old tongue of the Arkasodara, his name means “heavenly light” or simply “eye”─a reference to his ability to discern good and evil."
msgstr "Механическая статуя ДайвадИпы, одного из божеств мургов, которым издавна поклоняются на Тавнаире. На древнем языке аркасодара его имя означает «небесный свет» или просто «глаз» — намёк на способность отличать добро от зла."

#. ja: 見抜イタ！
#. de: Meinen großen Augen entgeht nichts!<br><i>Gyoka</i>
#. fr: Le bien, le mal<nbsp>!
#. column 0: Summon your wind-up Daivadipa minion. Can discern good and evil─so long as they are at knee height.
#. column 1: A mechanical image of Daivadipa, one of the Mrga traditionally worshipped in Thavnair. In the old tongue of the Arkasodara, his name means “heavenly light” or simply “eye”─a reference to his ability to discern good and evil.
#. column 3: Divine Eye
