#. ja: ミニオン「モロコシ様」を呼び出す。<br>古い精霊を自称するトウモロコシのような何か。はらへりを見過ごせない！
#. de: Du rufst Meister Mais als Begleiter herbei. Gebieter aus alten Zeiten oder ein einfacher Maiskolben? Das ist hier die Frage.
#. fr: Vous appelez votre mascotte sire Épidemaïs, un étrange personnage ayant l'apparence d'un épi de maïs, pour le moins appétissant, et qui prétend être un esprit ancien.
#. column 1: At the conclusion of your travels with the Cornservant, the corn-shaped spirit that provides sustenance to the hungry, the being quietly left one of its kernels in your bag. That kernel quickly grew into another Cornservant, which ever regards you anxiously, worried that you might require a feed.
#. column 2: Where there are those in need<br>of sustenance, I will be there.<br>   - The Cornservant
#. column 3: Well Fed
#. column 4: Restores 100 HP to all allies within range (150 if the ally is a <ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>critter</ui-edge-color></ui-color>).
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:516:0:0"
msgid "Summon your Cornservant minion. Will never let you go hungry."
msgstr "Призвать прислужника «Кукурузный слуга». Он никогда не даст тебе проголодаться."

#. ja: 自らの実を分け与え、はらへりの民を満腹にすべく旅するトウモロコシの精霊を自称する何か。別れ際、そっとカバンに投げ込まれた一粒の実が、あれよあれよと立派な精霊に成長。冒険者が飢えないか心配な様子である
#. de: Ein mysteriöser Maiskolben, der sich überall als Gebieter aus alten Zeiten vorstellt, reist umher, um Maisgerichte aus eigenem Anbau an die Hungrigen zu verteilen. Nach eurer Verabschiedung hatte er ein Maiskorn in deinen Beutel geworfen, das seinerseits zu einem Maisgeist heranwuchs und dich seither begleitet<nbsp>... für den Fall, dass du auf deinen Abenteuern hungrig wirst.
#. fr: À l'origine, cet étrange personnage serait un esprit lié au maïs, qui voyage un peu partout afin de nourrir les gens affamés en leur donnant de ses grains. Celui qui vous accompagne est apparu après que sire Épidemaïs a jeté un grain dans votre sac lorsqu'il a pris congé de vous. Il semble s'inquiéter que vous puissiez avoir faim.
#. column 0: Summon your Cornservant minion. Will never let you go hungry.
#. column 2: Where there are those in need<br>of sustenance, I will be there.<br>   - The Cornservant
#. column 3: Well Fed
#. column 4: Restores 100 HP to all allies within range (150 if the ally is a <ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>critter</ui-edge-color></ui-color>).
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:516:0:1"
msgid "At the conclusion of your travels with the Cornservant, the corn-shaped spirit that provides sustenance to the hungry, the being quietly left one of its kernels in your bag. That kernel quickly grew into another Cornservant, which ever regards you anxiously, worried that you might require a feed."
msgstr "Когда путешествие с Кукурузным слугой, духом в облике кукурузного початка, который кормит голодных, подошло к концу, тот тайком оставил тебе в сумке одно зёрнышко. Оно быстро выросло в нового Кукурузного слугу, который теперь тревожно поглядывает на тебя — вдруг тебе понадобится подкрепиться."

#. ja: ふぃ～
#. de: Pop, pop!
#. fr: Pop pop<nbsp>!
#. column 0: Summon your Cornservant minion. Will never let you go hungry.
#. column 1: At the conclusion of your travels with the Cornservant, the corn-shaped spirit that provides sustenance to the hungry, the being quietly left one of its kernels in your bag. That kernel quickly grew into another Cornservant, which ever regards you anxiously, worried that you might require a feed.
#. column 3: Well Fed
#. column 4: Restores 100 HP to all allies within range (150 if the ally is a <ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>critter</ui-edge-color></ui-color>).
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:516:0:2"
msgid "Where there are those in need<br>of sustenance, I will be there.<br>   - The Cornservant"
msgstr "Я буду рядом,<br>если кто-то проголодался.<br>   — Кукурузный слуга"

#. ja: まんぷく
#. de: Sattmacher
#. fr: Rassasiement
#. column 0: Summon your Cornservant minion. Will never let you go hungry.
#. column 1: At the conclusion of your travels with the Cornservant, the corn-shaped spirit that provides sustenance to the hungry, the being quietly left one of its kernels in your bag. That kernel quickly grew into another Cornservant, which ever regards you anxiously, worried that you might require a feed.
#. column 2: Where there are those in need<br>of sustenance, I will be there.<br>   - The Cornservant
