msgstr "Устанавливает ловушку, которая при срабатывании наносит всем врагам в радиусе действия урон силой 260.<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Задержка срабатывания:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 10 сек."

#. ja: ミニオン「ティンセントリーT1」を呼び出す。<br>未来の兵士をイメージして作られた、数百年前の玩具人形
#. de: Du rufst deinen Zinnwächter T1 als Begleiter herbei. Dieses Spielzeug bietet einen jahrhundertealten Blick in die Zukunft.
#. fr: Vous appelez votre mascotte sentinelle de plomb T1, un jouet créé il y a plusieurs centaines d'années en imaginant les soldats du futur.
#. column 1: This toy soldier was popular centuries ago in the Alexandria of old. Legend has it the living Sphene was gifted one by a child she met when she had snuck into town, and it became the basis for the design of the mechanical soldiers that were developed shortly thereafter.
#. column 2: It's time we gave that new toy<br>of yours a proper field test.<br>   - Cid
#. column 3: Kingdom Defense
#. column 4: Delivers an attack with a potency of 230 to all enemies within range.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:522:0:0"
msgid "Summon your tin sentry T1 minion. It's your own fault if you get hit."
msgstr "Призвать прислужника «Оловянный часовой Т1». Если тебя ударят, сам виноват."

#. ja: 数百年前にアレクサンドリアで流行したブリキ製の玩具人形。生前のスフェーンがお忍びで街に出かけた際に、子どもから贈られたことがあり、のちに機械兵を開発する際に外装デザインの参考とされたらしい
#. de: Ein Spielzeug aus Blech, das sich vor hunderten von Jahren in Alexandria größter Beliebheit erfreute. Es soll Königin Sphene einst von einem Kind geschenkt worden sein und wurde später bei der Entwicklung der Maschinensoldaten als optische Vorlage verwendet.
#. fr: Ce jouet a connu un grand succès il y a plusieurs centaines d'années à Alexandrie. La reine Sphene en aurait reçu un de la part d'un enfant lors de l'une de ses escapades en ville, et celui-ci aurait ensuite servi de modèle pour l'apparence des sentinelles mécaniques lors de leur conception.
#. column 0: Summon your tin sentry T1 minion. It's your own fault if you get hit.
#. column 2: It's time we gave that new toy<br>of yours a proper field test.<br>   - Cid
#. column 3: Kingdom Defense
#. column 4: Delivers an attack with a potency of 230 to all enemies within range.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:522:0:1"
msgid "This toy soldier was popular centuries ago in the Alexandria of old. Legend has it the living Sphene was gifted one by a child she met when she had snuck into town, and it became the basis for the design of the mechanical soldiers that were developed shortly thereafter."
msgstr "Этот игрушечный солдатик был популярен в древней Александрии несколько столетий назад. По легенде, когда Сфина была ещё жива, ребёнок, с которым она познакомилась во время тайной прогулки по городу, подарил ей такого солдатика. Вскоре после этого его внешний вид послужил образцом для механических воинов."

#. ja: カションカション
#. de: Kaschung, kaschung!
#. fr: Bviiih, bviiih<nbsp>!
#. column 0: Summon your tin sentry T1 minion. It's your own fault if you get hit.
#. column 1: This toy soldier was popular centuries ago in the Alexandria of old. Legend has it the living Sphene was gifted one by a child she met when she had snuck into town, and it became the basis for the design of the mechanical soldiers that were developed shortly thereafter.
#. column 3: Kingdom Defense
#. column 4: Delivers an attack with a potency of 230 to all enemies within range.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:522:0:2"
msgid "It's time we gave that new toy<br>of yours a proper field test.<br>   - Cid"
msgstr "Пора как следует испытать<br>твою новую игрушку в деле.<br>   — Сид"

#. ja: 王国防衛
#. de: Verteidigung des Königreichs
#. fr: Défense du royaume
#. column 0: Summon your tin sentry T1 minion. It's your own fault if you get hit.
#. column 1: This toy soldier was popular centuries ago in the Alexandria of old. Legend has it the living Sphene was gifted one by a child she met when she had snuck into town, and it became the basis for the design of the mechanical soldiers that were developed shortly thereafter.
#. column 2: It's time we gave that new toy<br>of yours a proper field test.<br>   - Cid
#. column 4: Delivers an attack with a potency of 230 to all enemies within range.
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:522:0:3"
msgid "Kingdom Defense"
msgstr "Защита королевства"

#. ja: 範囲内にいる敵に、ATK230のダメージを与える。
#. de: Führt eine Attacke mit Attacke-Wert 230 auf die Gegner in der Nähe aus.
#. fr: Inflige des dégâts d'attaque 230 aux ennemis dans l'aire d'effet.
#. column 0: Summon your tin sentry T1 minion. It's your own fault if you get hit.
#. column 1: This toy soldier was popular centuries ago in the Alexandria of old. Legend has it the living Sphene was gifted one by a child she met when she had snuck into town, and it became the basis for the design of the mechanical soldiers that were developed shortly thereafter.
#. column 2: It's time we gave that new toy<br>of yours a proper field test.<br>   - Cid
#. column 3: Kingdom Defense
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:522:0:4"
msgid "Delivers an attack with a potency of 230 to all enemies within range."
msgstr "Наносит всем врагам в радиусе действия урон силой 230."

#. ja: ミニオン「検証体アンブローズ」を呼び出す。<br>実験体アンブローズの開発過程で生み出された小型検証体
#. de: Du rufst deinen Ambrose-Prototyp als Begleiter herbei. An seinen Eigenheiten merkt man, dass es sich um ein Versuchsmodell handelt.
#. fr: Vous appelez votre mascotte Ambrose prototype, un modèle réduit qui a été conçu lors du développement et de la con<shy>struc<shy>tion d'Ambrose.
#. column 1: The researchers of Origenics created this miniaturized prototype in order to ascertain the effects of excess soul use in their latest test subject. For this purpose, the souls of small animals were infused into the unit, which may explain its tendency to follow after people.
#. column 2: I'm only here because of<br>unfinished business.<br>   - Aldis
#. column 3: Under Testing
#. column 4: Delivers an attack with a potency of 70 to all enemies within range while reducing movement speed by 50%.<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Duration:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 10s
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:523:0:0"
msgid "Summon your Ambrose the Unfinished minion. Unfinished it may be, but it is certainly not unwilling."
msgstr "Призвать прислужника «Амброуз-недоделка». Он может и не закончен, но уж точно не против."

#. ja: 実験体アンブローズの開発過程で生み出された小型検証体。魂資源の過剰投入による反応を確認するため、まずは小さな本機を生成し、小動物の魂を使った検証を行ったらしい。人の後を付け回すのも、その影響だろうか
#. de: Dieses verkleinerte Modell wurde während der Entwicklung und Herstellung von Ambrose entworfen, um die Reaktion auf den übermäßigen Gebrauch von Seelen zu testen. Für dieses Modell wurden dafür die Seelen von kleinen Tieren verwendet. Wahrscheinlich ist dieses Experiment auch der Grund dafür, dass diese Miniaturausgabe dich auf Schritt und Tritt begleitet.
#. fr: Ce modèle réduit a été conçu lors du développement et de la fabrication d'Ambrose, notamment pour vérifier la réaction provoquée par l'utilisation excessive d'âmes en employant celles de petits animaux avec cette maquette. D'ailleurs, c'est pro<shy>ba<shy>ble<shy>ment à cause de cette expérience que cet appareil miniature vous suit partout.
#. column 0: Summon your Ambrose the Unfinished minion. Unfinished it may be, but it is certainly not unwilling.
#. column 2: I'm only here because of<br>unfinished business.<br>   - Aldis
#. column 3: Under Testing
#. column 4: Delivers an attack with a potency of 70 to all enemies within range while reducing movement speed by 50%.<br><ui-color 504><ui-edge-color 505>Duration:</ui-edge-color></ui-color> 10s
msgctxt "CompanionTransient:523:0:1"
msgid "The researchers of Origenics created this miniaturized prototype in order to ascertain the effects of excess soul use in their latest test subject. For this purpose, the souls of small animals were infused into the unit, which may explain its tendency to follow after people."
msgstr "Исследователи Оридженикса создали этот миниатюрный прототип, чтобы изучить последствия чрезмерного использования душ на испытуемом. В куклу вложили души мелких животных — возможно, поэтому она так любит ходить за людьми."

